    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1190-a1">

                <pb facs="1067" n="753" xml:id="pg753"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>

                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 5, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>572. Your 718. Department will be glad to submit any proposals that the German
                    Government may care to make to other belligerents, looking to an arrangement as
                    to what should be given prisoners of war in nature of food and clothing.
                    Department can do nothing unless requested by the belligerents.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
